Package: RobustSandwichRV
Type: Package
Title: Certified Robustness Values with Sandwich Standard Errors
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jan", "Acedanski", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "robustsandwichrv@users.noreply.github.com"),
    person("OpenAI", role = "ctb")
  )
Description: Computes sample robustness values for omitted-variable
    sensitivity analysis in linear regression when inference uses classical,
    HC0, HC1, CR0, or CR1 standard errors. Implements point-conditioned and
    benchmark-bounded calibration, analytical protected lower bounds,
    constructive confounder witnesses, and independent full-regression
    validation. The package uses Cinelli-Hazlett partial-R-squared geometry
    but explicitly accounts for attainable sandwich standard-error ratios.
